===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|cariatide}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|caryatides}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|Καρυάτιδες|}}, plural of {{m|grc|Καρυᾶτις||a priestess of Artemis, female figures used as bearing-shafts}}, from {{m|grc|Καρυατίζω||dance the Karyatid festival dance}} from {{m|grc|Καρύαι||a town in Laconia with a temple of Artemis and a festival}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A sculpted female figure serving as an [[architectural]] element, used as a support for [[entablature]].

